+# Working with Rojo day to day
+
+Git is the source of truth. The place in Studio is a build of this repo, and `rojo serve` keeps it
+in sync with the files. The README's Layout table shows which folder becomes which part of the
+place.
+
+## First-time setup
+
+1. Install the tools with Rokit (`rokit install`). Use the `rojo` from `rokit.toml`, and a Rojo
+   Studio plugin that matches its version.
+2. Install packages: `pesde install` in the repo root, then again in `test_packages/` for Jest.
+3. Make your own dev place: publish a fresh Baseplate to your own account or group. Never serve
+   into a shared or live place.
+4. Add your dev place's id to `servePlaceIds` in `default.project.json` in a small commit of its
+   own. Rojo then refuses to live-sync into any place that isn't on the list.
+
+## Daily loop
+
+1. Pull `main` and branch off it. Stop `rojo serve` before you `pull`, `checkout`, `rebase`,
+   `stash`, or `pesde install`. Those rewrite many watched files at once.
+2. Run `rojo serve` in the repo root (port 34872). Open your dev place and click **Connect** in
+   the Rojo plugin.
+3. Edit files under `src/` in your editor. Saving a file pushes it into Studio.
+4. Test in Studio: run the Jest specs and playtest.
+5. Before you push, run the checks in the README (sourcemap, `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene`,
+   `stylua --check`). Check that `git status` lists only the files you meant to change.
+
+## Where changes go
+
+- **Make code changes in files, never in Studio.** The next sync overwrites a script you edit in
+  Studio, and Git never sees the edit. The same goes for properties, attributes, tags, and new
+  instances under a synced folder.
+- Attributes and tags go in a `Name.meta.json` beside the file, or in `init.meta.json` inside a
+  folder.
+- Models and GUIs you build in Studio go back into Git as an `.rbxm` (**Save to File**) over the
+  file they came from.
+- Don't edit `roblox_packages/` or `test_packages/roblox_packages/`. pesde replaces them on every
+  install. Change a dependency in `pesde.toml` and reinstall.
+- Require packages through their links (`ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Vide`), never through a
+  `.pesde/...` path.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Is the server still running?** Rojo 7.7.0 and 7.7.1 can crash when a file or folder is deleted,
+  moved, or renamed. When that happens, Studio quietly stops getting your changes. After any of
+  those, look for `Rojo crashed!` in the terminal. Restart `rojo serve` if it stopped, then
+  reconnect.
+- **Did your change arrive?** Open the script in Studio and confirm it shows your new code before
+  you trust a test or playtest. If an error's line number didn't move after your edit, Studio is
+  still running the old code.
+- **Which code are you running?** Your dev place runs whatever the connected server serves: that
+  folder, on whatever branch is checked out there. A merged pull request isn't in your place until
+  you pull it.
+- If the plugin reports a protocol version mismatch, update the plugin to match the project's
+  Rojo version.
+
+## Keeping `default.project.json` healthy
+
+This file decides where everything goes in the place. One bad merge here can move Jest's packages
+or empty out a service without any error. To keep it healthy:
+
+- Change it only when the README's Layout table changes too, and in the same commit. The table is
+  the spec.
+- **Resolving a conflict:** don't just accept both sides. Rebuild the tree so it matches the Layout
+  table. Each node must appear exactly once, and every `$path` must name a folder that exists.
+  Typos such as `StarterPlayerScript` mount nothing.
+- Leave the `Tests` node and the `globIgnorePaths` entry together. `Tests.Packages` (Jest) must stay
+  under `ServerScriptService.Tests`, because specs require `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages.Jest`.
+- Save it as UTF-8 **without a byte order mark**, or Rojo fails at line 1. Windows PowerShell's
+  `Set-Content` and `Out-File` add one, so edit the file in your editor.
+- Before you push a change to it, run
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`. Then confirm that
+  `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`, `ReplicatedStorage.Packages`, and
+  `StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts` all appear in the sourcemap with children.
+- Get a second reviewer on any pull request that touches it.
